      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c40d348e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: dad_what_is_losing; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a father being asked by his son what 'losing' means, and the father responds by claiming he doesn't know because he is a Trump supporter. This juxtaposition is intended to satirize or mock individuals who support Donald Trump by implying that their political affiliation renders them incapable of understanding basic concepts like 'losing'. The intent is to portray Trump supporters as intellectually or morally deficient, which can be harmful as it promotes a negative stereotype and may contribute to social division or hostility toward this group. The meme does not contain explicit abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements, but it does contain harmful content by stigmatizing a political group based on their beliefs, potentially reinforcing prejudice and polarization.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3ef835e0"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
